{"result":"{
  "id": "18432",
  "key": "SFCC-236",
  "summary": "Product Card Shared Component",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18432",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n\n**I want** product cards to display relevant information for the surface I am browsing, \n\n**so that** each page feels appropriately tailored without inconsistent component implementations across the site.\n\n----\n\n**Images for reference (Figma is leading):**\n\n![\"image-20260727-234551.png\"](image-20260727-234551.png)\n\n\n\nThis story covers the build of a single shared Product Card component that supports multiple display variations via a style prop. Each variation controls which elements are shown — the component itself is built and maintained once. The component is scoped to the visual and interactive layer only — product data is sourced from SFCC. \n\n**Variations in scope:** \n\n- Homepage\n- PLP\n- Wish List\n- Recently Viewed",
  "status": {
    "name": "In Progress",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "High"
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
    "name": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
    "email": "marcel.a.n.navarro@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/482e2e100517026f4980d6455214aa11?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMN-6.png"
  },
  "reporter": {
    "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Custom",
    "PRC-09",
    "SPR-01",
    "SPR-02",
    "SPR-10",
    "SPR-11",
    "SPR-12",
    "SPR-13",
    "SPR-14",
    "SPR-16",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "created": "2026-07-24T13:49:49.338+1000",
  "updated": "2026-09-02T12:59:43.280+1000",
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13665",
      "body": "User:712020:c99d37b3-9c93-4347-951d-5ffb32ff1341 User:712020:4ec4770e-9470-4885-9753-69a36b6cf950 The product card user story is ready for your review - I’ll assign to Emma first. \n\nThe product card behaviour on the ‘see full recently viewed’ page was not specified in the design - I asked Kiera - she recommended to keep the behaviour similar to product card on PLP. I have written the story in that way - if you expect the product card to behave differently on the see full recently viewed page, please let me know the desired behaviour and I’ll update the AC.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-04T15:42:25.807+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-04T15:42:25.807+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13804",
      "body": "hi User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d \n\nFirst to answer you question regarding the behaviour on the ‘see full recently viewed’ page - I believe the behaviour should be consistent with the product card on PLP. User:60d1a439f65054006947ea0d or User:712020:4ec4770e-9470-4885-9753-69a36b6cf950 correct me if your expectation is different.\n\nNext on the AC’s:\n\n**PLP variation**\n\n- Whats been listed seems correct but can you confirm if the interactions when the client clicks on the bag, or selects a size (mobile and desktop) are captured on another ticket?\n      - If yes this section is approved if no then they need to be added\n\n**Home page variation**\n\n- User:712020:4ec4770e-9470-4885-9753-69a36b6cf950 I assume it is correct that the bag should be excluded from homepage, so if a client wants to add to bag they must click on the product tile (image, name) so that they land on the PDP for that product\n\n**Wishlist variation**\n\nApproved\n\n**Recently Viewed Full History variation (same behavior as PLP card)**\n\n- open questions above to be confirmed.\n\n**Variation extensibility**\n\nAgreed",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "name": "Emma Kirwan",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/437c30dd63bbb0ec0a2f7c0d8d556d93?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FEK-4.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-11T21:43:46.515+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-11T21:43:46.515+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13812",
      "body": "User:712020:c99d37b3-9c93-4347-951d-5ffb32ff1341 Yes, we will cover the behaviour of the product card component also in each page (please note some of these are still draft stories):\n[SFCC-185 PLP UI – Quick Add to Bag - Jira](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-185)\n[SFCC-497 Wishlist – Add to Bag Icon / CTA - Jira](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-497)\n[SFCC-84](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-84) \n[SFCC-90 Homepage Layout & Content Modules UI - Jira](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-90)\n\nI will link all of these as related tickets.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-12T09:39:18.300+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-12T09:39:18.300+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13880",
      "body": "User:712020:c99d37b3-9c93-4347-951d-5ffb32ff1341 User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d Please see my notes below:\n\nCore component:\n\n- We don’t want the product badge to render in all locations. PLP, the Full History of Recently Viewed and in the Wishlist is ok. We do not want the badge displayed on the Homepage or on the Recently Viewed product carousel at the bottom of pages. If we place products on an editorial or landing page we also wouldn’t want the badge applied. \n- Similarly, we don’t want the hover action (model photo( on the homepage or the recently viewed carousel at the bottom of the pages.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Dani Rivett",
        "name": "Dani Rivett",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/42d3d7910c25b8f4ba9e46aabfc6c149?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDR-3.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-14T17:02:13.918+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-14T17:02:13.918+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13891",
      "body": "User:712020:4ec4770e-9470-4885-9753-69a36b6cf950 Thanks for your review.\nI am updating the following AC, change is green, red is removed.\n\\*\\*Core Component\\*\\*\n1. Given a product is passed to the card component, when it renders, then the primary product image is and product name are always displayed regardless of variation.\n1. Given a product has a badge (e.g. Runway), when the card renders in any variation, then the badge is displayed in the correct position per Figma.\n1. Given the card renders, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the tile image switches from the item/flat photo to the model photo.\n\\*\\*PLP Variation\\*\\*\n1. Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the size selector becomes visible and the price disappears and the tile image switches from the item/flat photo to the model photo.\n\\*\\*Home page variation\\*\\*\n1. Given the card renders on home page, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, and badge are displayed.\n\\*\\*Wishlist variation\\*\\*\n1. Given the card renders on wishlist, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the tile image switches from the item/flat photo to the model photo.\n1. Given the card renders on wishlist, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n\\*\\*Recently Viewed Full History variation (same behavior as PLP card)\\*\\*\n1. Given the card renders on recently viewed full history page, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the size selector becomes visible and the price disappears and the tile image switches from the item/flat photo to the model photo.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-17T12:05:25.400+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-17T12:07:39.970+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "14050",
      "body": "⚠️ All DoR checklist items must be completed before moving this issue forward. The issue has been moved back automatically. \n\nUser:5f506d223e9e2e004d7c48ac  Please complete all items in the checklist and try again.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Automation for Jira",
        "name": "Automation for Jira",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/600529a9c8bfef89daa848e6db28ed2d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAJ-0.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-26T11:10:52.681+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-26T11:10:52.681+1000"
    }
  ]
}"}

