      "summary": "PWA Kit Components",
      "description": "Epic Summary\nBuild and maintain the shared UI component library for the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. This covers foundational design system elements — typography, icons, logo, colour tokens, and reusable UI components — that are consumed across all frontend epics.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nA consistent, well-documented component library ensures visual consistency across all 8 storefronts and speeds up frontend development by giving Squad B a shared set of building blocks to work from rather than rebuilding common elements per page.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nUI component library setup (typography, icons, logo, colour tokens)\nReusable PWA Kit components consumed across frontend epics\nOut of Scope:\nMotion design guidelines and animation behaviour — covered in Motion Design (SFCC-86)\nPage-level layout and feature build — covered in their respective epics (PDP, PLP, Homepage, etc.)\nSFCC Business Manager configuration — covered in Platform Setup (SFCC-1)\nDependencies\nSFCC-1 (Platform Setup & Environments) — PWA Kit scaffold must be in place\nFigma design assets and design handoff from Zimmermann design team\nAssumptions & Constraints\nComponent library serves all 8 storefronts with regional variations handled at the page/epic level\nZimmermann design team provides Figma files as the source of truth for component specs",
